\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces HTB shaping hierarchy on the UPF egress interface. URLLC carries \texttt {prio\nobreakspace {}1} (strict priority), ensuring URLLC packets skip the queue whenever aggregate utilisation approaches the physical ceiling.\relax }}{23}{figure.caption.27}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces Closed-loop orchestrator control flow. Both orchestrator types share the Observe–Validate–Act–Reflect structure. The agentic system additionally invokes the Memory Agent and produces a Chain-of-Thought reasoning trace.\relax }}{24}{figure.caption.29}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces Column schema of the six collected datasets (rule-based $\times $ \{low, medium, high\} and agentic $\times $ \{low, medium, high\}). Each row is one 3-second control cycle. The agentic-specific columns (\texttt {root\_cause\_assessment}, \texttt {lever\_validity\_score}, \texttt {wla\_activated}, \texttt {memory\_*}) are populated only in agentic runs; rule-based runs carry equivalent synthetic labels for paired comparison.\relax }}{25}{figure.caption.30}%
